{
  "schemaVersion": 2,
  "id": "volatility-ranking",
  "title": "Volatility Ranking",
  "turns": [
    {
      "jobId": "07df4867-026c-4d03-9f6c-cb322e9a367b",
      "question": "Among the 1,000 most liquid US stocks, which five had the highest and which five the lowest daily volatility from January 2, 2025 through January 30, 2026, and what were their returns over that period?",
      "submittedAt": "2026-10-06T23:57:04.050683Z",
      "completedAt": "2026-10-06T23:57:17.485274Z",
      "status": "success",
      "report": {
        "markdown": "**Highest daily volatility (top 5 of 1,000 most liquid stocks, Jan 2 2025 – Jan 30 2026)**\n\n| Rank | Ticker | Daily volatility | Return over period |\n|------|--------|------------------|---------------------|\n| 1 | DFDV | 74.6% | 4,656% |\n| 2 | BMNR | 54.4% | 247% |\n| 3 | DGNX | 49.9% | 917% |\n| 4 | ABVX | 35.9% | 1,425% |\n| 5 | ASST | 30.5% | 55.0% |\n\n[1]\n\n**Lowest daily volatility (bottom 5 of 1,000 most liquid stocks, same window)**\n\n| Rank | Ticker | Daily volatility | Return over period |\n|------|--------|------------------|---------------------|\n| 1 | BTT | 0.37% | 10.5% |\n| 2 | BTZ | 0.63% | 1.33% |\n| 3 | BBN | 0.64% | 1.18% |\n| 4 | AWF | 0.67% | –0.37% |\n| 5 | DLY | 0.71% | –7.09% |\n\n[2]\n\n**Notes**\n- Volatility is the daily standard deviation of returns; returns run from the close before the first session (Jan 2 2025) to the last close (Jan 30 2026). Both are shown as percentages (the tool returns fractions).\n- The universe is the 1,000 most liquid U.S. stocks (`liquid_1000`); 993 assets had sufficient data to be ranked.\n- BMNR only traded for ~61% of the sessions (coverage ratio 0.61), so its figures reflect a partial period.\n\n## Sources\n\n- [1] Market analytics result — market scan — evidence `hermes-receipt:22a8eadf01cc90443a253facaf6efed621970a56314045c5f99ac9ea66ea6f09`\n- [2] Market analytics result — market scan — evidence `hermes-receipt:8b5ae40d33a66104f41ed2dca04dcab642df00c18a1808085676dc0eebd8a1f4`",
